---
// Invisalign Service Page - Central Dentist
import ServicePageMinimal from '../../layouts/ServicePageMinimal.astro';

const content = `Straight teeth are about more than aesthetics. Optimal tooth alignment supports improved oral hygiene, reduces the risk of infection and gum disease, promotes proper jaw positioning to minimize clenching and grinding, and can even improve sleep quality by addressing sleep-disordered breathing.

At Central Dentist, our doctors have advanced training in comprehensive orthodontics from the United States Dental Institute, and we have found Invisalign to be an effective tool for many of our adult patients seeking efficient orthodontic outcomes. Individual treatment time varies based on each patient's needs.

Invisalign clear aligners are virtually invisible and removable, meaning they integrate seamlessly into your daily life without disrupting your professional career or oral health routine. They are typically more comfortable than traditional braces and contribute to far less inflammation in the body than any metal-based technique.

Invisalign also leverages artificial intelligence and machine learning, drawing on millions of cases worldwide to optimize every treatment plan. This means your aligners are designed using the collective wisdom of one of the largest orthodontic databases in the world, resulting in more predictable outcomes and faster treatment times.

Our lead provider, Dr. Jill Ombrello, is a member of the American Academy of Clear Aligners (AACA), which means she has received advanced training in Invisalign case management and is part of a collaborative network of providers who share expertise. Combined with her background in holistic oral health through the International Academy of Oral Medicine and Toxicology (IAOMT), her experience with sleep, airway, and TMJ health, and her undergraduate training in physical therapy, Dr. Jill brings a comprehensive perspective to every Invisalign case.

For many of our patients, Dr. Jill is able to achieve outcomes in as little as 4 months, though individual results and treatment times vary. As part of your comprehensive new patient exam, you'll receive a personalized Invisalign consultation and smile simulation, allowing you to preview your potential results and determine whether clear aligners are the right fit for your smile goals.

*Your personalized Invisalign consultation and smile simulation are included as part of your comprehensive new patient exam. New patient exam fees, diagnostic imaging, x-rays, and any recommended treatment are billed separately. Please contact our office for current exam pricing.*`;

const benefits = [
  'Nearly invisible, removable clear aligners',
  'Treatment in as little as 4 months for some patients (individual results vary)',
  'Improved oral hygiene during treatment',
  'AI-powered treatment planning from millions of cases',
  'AACA-certified provider (Dr. Jill Ombrello)',
  'Holistic approach considering airway and TMJ health',
  'Comfortable, with no metal brackets or wires',
  'Personalized Invisalign consultation with digital smile simulation'
];
